From: ultimatejeeves <ultimatejeeves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:38:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/43] VM: keep the emulated clock on the wall clock by
 skipping EE cycles (catch-up); EE/VU1 debug counters

Time the EE thread waits on the VPU1/GS threads, and time it can't emulate fast enough, no longer slows the
whole console down: the cycles it is behind by are counted as run (bounded), so games drop frames at full
speed. getEeStats, VU1 pc/disassembly for the bench, game frame counter (newFrames).
